1505:- Ready to call (`call.ready`) — Order details + View Rx, medicines, notes (no script card before Call — D-58 pt 18, D-71): **Call patient** · Header Back → "Leave this case?" sheet: **Release case** / **Stay** (D-58 pt 20, OQ-024; label D-84 CA-22) — *Source: App logic §4.*
1547:- **Empty case (D-80 pt 4, D-81 F23, D-83):** no **Call patient**. An amber notice at the top of the panel says "No medicines on this order. Our Ops team will check it." (D-84; was "This order has no medicines. Release it — our Ops team will check it.") (where the released case goes is open, OQ-035). The main button is **Release case**, which releases directly (Releasing…, no sheet) and returns the doctor to Home. Header Back does the same. When Order details is hidden, View Rx is left-aligned. — *Source: App logic §4.*
1554:- **Call ended, outcome card (D-81 F26, retired D-83):** the "End the call to get your next case." warning is retired with state 15b; after the hang-up the card is title only, neutral (MAIN-CHECK 2, D-85; `call.forwardedAfterHangup` retired, §14). — *Source: App logic §4.*
1568:- **Leaving a case:** the back-blocked toast breaks between its two sentences. An **attempted call** = leg 2 answered (the patient picked up) (D-58). Once a call is attempted, leaving is blocked until the case is closed (callback, unavailable, confirm). Before that, header **Back** opens the "Leave this case?" sheet — **Release case** (the case returns to the queue) or **Stay** (D-58 point 20, OQ-024; label D-84 CA-22; on Ready and states 3 and 4 only). Header Back is on 1, 3 and 4 only, while the patient has never been reached. It is hidden from the **Call patient** / **Call again** tap, incl. Calling 7a, the 7b question, Transfer, and the callback sheets, and never returns once the patient answered, also on a later 3 / 4 (D-80 pt 1, D-81 F21). Behind the leave sheet, Releasing… and Release failed the screen is **Ready** (D-81 F22). The backend refuses Release once our call request is accepted, unless the result is 3 or 4 (D-80). Release returns the doctor to Home. If the patient answered just before the tap, the backend refuses the release and the doctor stays on the case (`a-release-failed`, "Couldn't release this case. You're still on it."). The unassign action itself is a backend dependency (OQ-024). Help stays available at every stage and is the way to reach Doctor Ops when something keeps failing. App closed or phone off mid-case → reopening goes straight back into the case `[OPEN OQ-025, backend]`. — *Source: App logic §4.*
1806:- 8c — `case.confirm-blocked`: Confirm tapped with Pending medicines · Tap on any confirm button while a medicine is Pending (Flag 5) · Confirm prescription only, plus a red line "Prescribe or disable {n} medicines first."; page scrolls to the first Pending medicine; button stays tappable; no Callback · `t08c-confirm-blocked` — *Source: App logic §5.*
1874:### case-55 · What happens in "retired (D-83, CW-E3)" (state 15b)?
1904:- Retired: `b-missed-call`, `b-didnt-connect` (sheets) — replaced by the automatic close and the notices. `a-leave-sheet` / `s7e-leave-sheet` is the approved Release sheet (D-58 point 20). The old state name **hold** for "didn't connect" is retired (old Flag 4). — *Source: App logic §5.*
1918:- **Dependency (Engineering):** the app gets call status by polling the backend (D-58 pt 19). Hiding Back once the patient answers and the transfer count both need **live** leg events from the partner during the call (leg 1 answered, leg 2 answered / Ozonetel `customerAnswered`), not only the result at the end (OQ-030). — *Source: App logic §5.*
1995:- **Transfer vs forward** (D-57): transfer = the patient is handed to an HA on the same call; forward = an HA calls the patient back separately. A failed transfer goes as a forward; after Transferring (13) the doctor sees state 15 `call.transfer-failed` — amber card "Forwarded to Health Advisor" with "Read the script, then end the call." (`call.transferFailed`) + script `call.forwardedTell` (§5, D-58 pts 17, 21, 23; MAIN-CHECK 2, D-85). A forward (15, B3) is confirmed only on the partner's result. — *Source: App logic §6.*
2014:### case-75 · What is the rule for "✅ Flag 5"?
2016:- ✅ **Flag 5 — answered:** Confirm is blocked while any medicine is Pending. The button stays tappable; on tap a notice in the bar says "Prescribe or disable {n} medicines first." and the page scrolls to the first Pending medicine. Applies to all three confirm buttons; Callback, Skip HA and Unavailable stay allowed. *Original flag:* The old code lets the doctor confirm while some medicines are still Pending (not prescribed, not disabled). No decision covers this. Options: (a) block Confirm until every medicine is Prescribed or Disabled, with a note saying how many are left; (b) allow it, and Pending medicines are dropped from the prescription; (c) allow it with a confirmation sheet. Recommendation: (a) — a prescription with unreviewed medicines is a clinical risk. — *Source: App logic §6.*
2084:### case-85 · What is the rule for "✅ Flag 6"?
2086:- ✅ **Flag 6 — answered:** the case does go back to the queue, but the doctor is not told — no queue line anywhere. **Updated D-83:** the case goes on hold and the system retries it by hangup cause; nothing goes to Ops. *Original flag:* the old code still opens an extra "unavailable" sheet with "Case will be reassigned to the queue". D-51 removed it; the rebuild follows D-51. Where the case goes after "unavailable" (back to the queue?) is not written in a decision — please confirm. — *Source: App logic §7.*
2121:- **Notes & symptoms** (D-59): Chief complaints / symptoms and Doctor notes, both optional. Editable from the moment the case opens until Confirm; typed text kept if the connection drops. **Saved only when the prescription is confirmed** — a case closed as Callback or Unavailable discards them (they are consultation notes, not a call log). Locked after Confirm. **Symptoms are printed on the prescription; Doctor notes are internal only** (doctor, HA, ops, pharmacy). — *Source: App logic §9.*
