   116	**How a call works (first release).** One telecom partner at a time (Ozonetel or Knowlarity), click-to-call. Doctor taps **Call patient** → the partner rings the **doctor's phone first** (leg 1) → then the **patient** (leg 2). The doctor talks and ends the call **on the phone**; there is **no End call in the app**. The partner reports leg 1 and leg 2 separately.
   117	
   118	**Rules**
   119	- **Gate time is a setting** (today 50 s). Every message reads it — no "50" hard-coded in copy.
   120	- **Talk time adds up** across connected calls on the same case (each at least ~10 s, within ~30 min) — D-58 point 22. The doctor is never shown the count.
   121	- **Attempted call** = leg 2 answered. A failed request, a doctor who didn't answer, or a patient who didn't answer is not an attempted call.
   122	- **Launch B, Pilot live call:** our app counts from the moment the patient answers, while the call is live; at the gate time **Confirm prescription** (B1) appears on the live call. Our count is the truth; the partner's duration is stored for reporting only. (**Transfer cases** — Confirm & transfer on the live call, Pilot Value Meds — are version A, later.)
   123	- **All other cases** (Cat4, HA skipped, and Pilot calls that end before the gate or have no result): the next actions unlock only when the partner's call result arrives after the call ends.
   124	- **Before the gate, never show:** Confirm prescription, Confirm & transfer, Confirm & forward, Skip HA.
   125	- **Patient-side failure** (leg 2: no answer, busy, rejected, switched off, unreachable, invalid number), whenever it is detected: the case closes as **Patient unavailable** (state 9) by itself and goes on **hold**; the system retries it by hangup cause (CW-B1, CW-B2). **Doctor-side failure** (the doctor's leg, or a request refused for a reason that isn't the patient's number) stays on 3 / 4 (CW-B1). The doctor gets **Request next case** on 9.
   126	- **Transfer** (15, B3): 15 = the transfer couldn't start (no HA free, or the request failed); the doctor is still on the line. An HA who doesn't pick up is 14 for the doctor (CW-E1). While the call is live, 15 and B3 show only "Waiting for the call to end…"; after the hang-up, **Request next case · Back to Home** (CW-E3). A forward (15, B3) is confirmed only on the partner's result (CW-F2). **Launch: Fallback B first** (CW-F1).
   127	- **A call that's too short** (state 6) offers **Call again · Callback** (D-58 point 23). No retry limit. **Callback is offered only after the call: on 6 and on 7d** (CW-A1, CW-C3). The backend refuses a callback unless the patient answered (leg 2) (CW-A1).
   128	- **No call result** (state 7, D-58 point 20): at 3 min the bar asks "Are you still on the call?" **only when the app can't know the call has ended** (CW-D1); when the partner has already reported the hang-up, the 3-min timeout goes straight to 7c. After "Call ended" and a backend check with nothing found: **Confirm prescription** (Cat4) or **Confirm & forward** (Pilot), with **Callback · Unavailable** (CW-D2). Confirm there shows "Waiting for the call record" until the record arrives (D-68); a record under the gate, or no record after a wait time, means the prescription is **not confirmed** → hold and retry (CW-D3, CW-D4). Nothing goes to Ops. A late result updates the screen by itself. Repeated problems → the doctor uses **Help** on the case.
   129	- **Callback on a live call is refused by the backend** unless the patient answered (leg 2); the sheet then shows "Couldn’t schedule a callback. The patient wasn’t reached." (CW-A1, K3).
   130	- **Vendor terms are mapped by Engineering** to the buckets in the table (Ozonetel `CustomerStatus`, Knowlarity hangup causes — `projects/ACOM/ring-ai/reference/knowlarity-hangup-causes.pdf`).
   131	
   132	**State table (final, 2026-10-24 — D-58 points 14–22; rows changed by the calling round are per D-83, see §14).** One row per state. Render id = recipe in `docs/renders/2026-10-22-calling/src/case.html`. Copy keys in `ui-screens/feedback/messages.json`. During every call the End-of-call script shows under Order details. Callback is offered only on 6 and 7d (D-83 CW-A1).
